WEBVTT

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.519
A beam of candlelight meets a

00:00:02.519 --> 00:00:03.685
glass prism.

00:00:03.685 --> 00:00:06.660
For centuries, one question split the

00:00:06.660 --> 00:00:08.833
world: what is light?

00:00:08.833 --> 00:00:12.793
Light is a wave. Watch how

00:00:12.793 --> 00:00:12.933
the

00:00:12.933 --> 00:00:16.833
ripples weave together.

00:00:16.833 --> 00:00:20.073
Through two narrow slits, my screen

00:00:20.073 --> 00:00:22.513
shows stripes.

00:00:22.513 --> 00:00:24.833
Only waves can do that.

00:00:24.833 --> 00:00:28.233
Yet light arrives in tiny packets,

00:00:28.233 --> 00:00:28.753
one quantum

00:00:28.753 --> 00:00:30.873
strikes the metal and an electron

00:00:30.873 --> 00:00:32.833
leaps out.

00:00:32.833 --> 00:00:36.413
So it travels like a wave

00:00:36.413 --> 00:00:40.833
and lands like a particle.

00:00:40.983 --> 00:00:43.008
Light is both — and that

00:00:43.008 --> 00:00:46.132
answer took three hundred years.
